{"archetypes":[{"name":"bash-fence","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The diff rewrites a shell orchestration fence where rc capture, set -e behavior, command substitution, and parsing order are easy to break.","prompt_body":"Investigate the Step 3.6 bash fence and driver routing for shell-control-flow bugs. Check rc capture under set -e, command-substitution output handling, case branching, heredoc/trailer parsing, and whether any failure path can accidentally continue or prompt. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"trailer-spoofing","focus_area":"security","weight":1,"rationale":"Trusted trailer parsing and untrusted assessor prose neutralization introduce a narrow spoofing boundary that needs specialist scrutiny.","prompt_body":"Investigate whether untrusted assessor output, verdict sidecars, or result env contents can influence trusted rc=10 control state. Focus on last-marker parsing, trailer filtering from display, neutralization of marker-like lines, fixed-key sidecar reads, and avoidance of source/eval/expansion. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"fd-quiet","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The change depends on the larch quiet FD contract, with user display moving through emit/FD 3 while stdout becomes logging.","prompt_body":"Investigate the FD and quiet-mode contract across the phase driver documentation, assessor driver, and tests. Check whether user-visible output consistently uses emit after quiet initialization, whether machine KVs are kept out of the display stream except trusted trailers, and whether tests exercise the same channel semantics as production. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"classification-gates","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The migration from workflow_path to design_classification crosses several scripts and can silently skip HARD assessment or snapshots if inconsistent.","prompt_body":"Investigate classification resolution across Step 3.6, assess-plan-round, and design-postplan-emit. Verify missing, invalid, and mismatched classification cases fail closed as HARD where required, SIMPLE skips only when truly intended, and legacy workflow_path cannot suppress required HARD behavior. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"resume-state","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"Step completion sentinels and pause handoff are being changed, which can cause resume to re-enter skipped work or bypass required assessor work.","prompt_body":"Investigate pause, resume, and completion-sentinel behavior around Step 3.6 and Gate-B-bypass paths. Check that pause-before-cheap-gate is preserved, rc=11 delegates pause saving exactly once, and every intentional bypass records the correct step completion state before Step 3b. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
